  "innovations_detailed": {
    "true_1m_context": "The MRCR v2 8-needle 'Long context retrieval' chart (shown ~1:15) plots Opus 4.6, Sonnet 4.6, Sonnet 4.5, GPT-5.4, and Gemini 3.1 Pro across 128K→1M input tokens. Degradation starts around 250K, but the Claude 4.6 line stays high across the full window while others fall off. The economic unlock is equally important: ONE price for the full window, no post-200K surcharge (Dan's long-standing complaint about Gemini). In Claude Code the 1M models are available by default. Enables long expertise files, whole-business context, and multi-round debate in a single session.",
    "customizable_agent_harness": "Pi (@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent) exposes an extension API with hooks (session_start, before_agent_start, input, message_end, tool_execution_start, tool_result), custom tool registration, subprocess control, persistent sessions, model registry, and TUI widgets/footers/themes. The CEO & Board is a single ~1,300-line TypeScript extension (apps/ceo/extensions/ceo-and-board.ts) plus 5 modules. It turns Pi into a deliberation engine: the CEO is the Pi agent itself (custom system prompt via before_agent_start); board members are Pi subprocesses. Dan notes it's ~2,000 lines total and admits it needs to be broken up ('2K lines is not a great design pattern').",
    "agent_expertise": "Expertise is declared in each agent's front matter (path, use-when, updatable). config.ts buildExpertiseBlock() renders each entry as a path + [read/write | read-only] + use-when line into {{EXPERTISE_BLOCK}} — it does NOT inline the file content; the agent reads/writes the file itself with its tools during the meeting. Persistence: expertise files live in .pi/ceo-agents/expertise/ and survive across deliberations (unlike the per-meeting session files). The CEO scratch pad tracks vote tallies, key insights, unresolved tensions, and an evolving thesis."
