  "system_architecture": {
    "summary": "A Pi extension turns the terminal into a one-shot deliberation engine. The CEO = the Pi agent itself, running a custom system prompt injected at before_agent_start. Board members = Pi subprocesses spawned with persistent sessions, each with its own system prompt, model, and expertise. Two custom tools (converse, end_deliberation) drive the meeting; a constraint engine bounds it; a synthwave TUI streams it live.",
    "ceo_is_the_pi_agent": "The CEO is not a subprocess. It is the primary Pi agent. On before_agent_start the extension reads .pi/ceo-agents/agents/ceo.md, builds expertise + skills blocks, string-replaces {{SESSION_ID}}, {{BRIEF_CONTENT}}, {{BOARD_MEMBERS}}, {{MEMO_PATH}}, {{MIN_TIME}}/{{MAX_TIME}}/{{MIN_BUDGET}}/{{MAX_BUDGET}}, and returns the assembled string as the systemPrompt. The CEO model (anthropic/claude-opus-4-6) is set from ceo.md front matter at session_start.",
    "board_members_are_subprocesses": "callBoardMember (modules/subprocess.ts) spawns `pi` with: --mode json -p --no-extensions --no-skills --no-prompt-templates --no-themes --session <file> --thinking off. On the FIRST call it also passes --system-prompt <resolved body> --model <model> and preloads context files via @<file> args. On later calls it passes only the session file + the CEO's message, so the persistent session carries full conversational context. Default board model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 (the 'Sonnet/Sonic' models). It parses the JSON event stream line-by-line: tool_execution_start, message_update/text_delta (live stream), message_end (usage: input/output tokens, cost.total, totalTokens).",
