# Brief: <concise title — frame as a question the board will answer>

## Situation
<What is happening right now? State the facts. No opinion, no spin. Include current state, key numbers, timeline, and what triggered this decision. Be specific — the board can't help without facts.>

## Stakes
<What's at risk? What's the upside if you get this right? What's the downside if you get it wrong? What happens if you do nothing? Be honest about magnitude — frame both sides of the bet.>

## Constraints
<List each constraint as a bullet. Be exhaustive — hidden constraints derail deliberations.>
- <Budget / financial limit>
- <Timeline / deadline>
- <Team capacity / headcount>
- <Technical / infrastructure>
- <Regulatory / legal / contractual>
- <Personal (health, family, location)>

## Key Question
<The single most important question you want the board to answer. One sentence. Be specific. "Should I X or Y given Z?" is better than "What should I do?">
