codex
The lesson architecture is now fixed: seven full teaching cycles rather than twelve shallow summaries. Each cycle will carry the complete required sequence—hook, model, source frame, named principle, worked course example, learner action, failure repair, current-practice overlay, retrieval, and teach-back—followed by the real five-part course-codebase lab. The `teach` skill specifically pushed the design toward repeated retrieval and durable skill checks, not transcript recognition.
apply patch
