105:          <li><strong>Productive disagreement</strong>Design specialists whose biases expose blind spots instead of producing eight versions of the same answer.</li>
111:        <p>The chapter follows the 40:03 lesson, its transcript, and the complete member course codebase at <code>agentic-horizon-extras/ceo-agents</code>. Exact model strings are recording-era details, not claims about the latest models. The lesson’s competitive claim about true one-million-token context is date-stamped. Two discrepancies between documentation and implementation are taught explicitly because the extension code is authoritative for runtime behavior.</p>
150:          <p>The lesson opens with a long-context retrieval chart. The point is not simply that a model accepts one million tokens. The point is how gracefully useful retrieval degrades as the input grows. Dan highlights the region around 250,000 tokens, then follows the lines toward one million. For this system, graceful degradation matters more than a marketing maximum because a forgotten constraint or lost dissent can change the decision.</p>
152:            <img src="../media/frames/ma-1-ceo-agents/t0076-1m-context-retrieval-chart.jpg" alt="Long context retrieval chart comparing recording-era models across input sizes from 128 thousand to one million tokens" width="3840" height="2160" loading="lazy">
637:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Why is disagreement a feature rather than a coordination failure?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Specialists are designed to expose different blind spots. Their conflict makes trade-offs visible and can improve the majority recommendation with conditions or tests.</p></details></div>
661:          <p>There is a second failure hiding nearby: documentation drift. A prompt says members answer sequentially. A README says the Contrarian always closes last. The UI does not prove either claim. If the system matters, the engineer must be able to move from statement to implementation to runtime evidence.</p>
702:              <tr><td>How does a round fan out?</td><td>The CEO prompt describes calls as sequential, with later members seeing earlier responses.</td><td><code>converse</code> launches selected members concurrently with <code>Promise.allSettled</code>. The extension does not sequentially feed returned answers from one target into the next.</td></tr>
703:              <tr><td>Does Contrarian close last?</td><td>README, prompt, and tool description say last is enforced.</td><td><code>end_deliberation</code> copies active members in configuration order and launches all final statements concurrently. Contrarian is fourth in the shipped roster, not a serialized final speaker.</td></tr>
704:              <tr><td>Are both minimums hard floors?</td><td>Configuration and explanatory copy present minimum time and budget as meeting floors.</td><td>The early-close guard programmatically checks minimum time. The v1 <code>end_deliberation</code> guard does not enforce <code>min_budget</code>.</td></tr>
707:          <p>The first check needs careful wording. Members are launched concurrently, so same-round answers are not deliberately piped into later members. Cross-round sharing is reliable because prompts tell members to reread the shared <code>conversation.jsonl</code>. Because that file is live, do not claim same-round cross-pollination is mechanically impossible; claim that it is not ordered or guaranteed. The portable mental model is <strong>concurrent within a round, reliably informed across rounds</strong>.</p>
726:          <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> two responses appear in a particular JSONL order, so you infer they were launched sequentially or that the later record necessarily read the earlier one.</p>
744:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. State the safest round-sharing model.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Selected members launch concurrently within a round, so ordered same-round cross-pollination is not guaranteed. Across rounds, members can reliably reread the shared conversation log.</p></details></div>
745:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. Name the three v1 gaps audited here.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Converse is concurrent rather than sequentially fed; Contrarian is not serialized last; and the early-close guard enforces minimum time but not minimum budget.</p></details></div>
998:            <li>Find the <code>Promise.allSettled</code> used by <code>converse</code>. Explain why this disproves a sequentially fed round.</li>
999:            <li>Find <code>allMembers = [...meetingState.activeMembers]</code> and the concurrent final-statement call. Explain why the shipped order does not enforce Contrarian last.</li>
1005:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul><li>6 points: correct log shape and bookend distinction.</li><li>6 points: concurrent launch explained from code without inferring dependency from completion order.</li><li>5 points: Contrarian-last discrepancy proven.</li><li>5 points: minimum-time versus minimum-budget enforcement proven.</li><li>3 points: CEO tool-use record located.</li></ul></div>
1035:          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">7. State the concurrent-round model precisely.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Targets launch concurrently, not as a sequential pipeline of returned answers. Same-round cross-pollination is not ordered or guaranteed; across rounds, members can reliably reread the shared log.</p></details></div>
1036:          <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">8. Name three runtime discrepancies a careful engineer should remember.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Converse is concurrent rather than sequentially fed; Contrarian is not serialized last; and minimum time is enforced by the close guard while minimum budget is not.</p></details></div>

